#N canvas 20 20 2600 1800 12;
#X text 20 20 g_grid -- the Launchpad's 108 addressable LEDs \, and their sole owner (C-5). g_oled's arbiter shape: layers with a priority and a time to live \, redrawn by a frame clock. ref/module/display.md, f 58;
#X text 20 170 creation arg 1: the Launchpad's Pd MIDI output port (1 on the device). inlet 0: surface ownership from m_launchpad \, 1 while in Programmer Mode. inlet 1: the beat number within the bar \, from u_root's c_clock. outlets: none., f 58;
#X text 20 320 One deviation from g_oled: home is a composite of regions \, the mode lamps along the top and the beat row along the bottom \, while modal and alert take the whole surface., f 58;
#X text 20 520 g_grid owns the LEDs and m_launchpad owns the mode. The first frame after ownership paints all 108 indices \, so that frame is the init clear., f 58;
#X obj 20 720 inlet;
#X obj 400 720 inlet;
#X obj 20 780 change -1;
#X obj 20 830 t f f;
#X obj 20 890 s \$0-own;
#X obj 200 890 select 1;
#X msg 200 940 1;
#X obj 200 990 s \$0-dirty;
#X obj 400 780 t f f;
#X obj 400 830 s \$0-beat;
#X msg 560 830 1;
#X obj 560 890 s \$0-dirty;
#X text 760 720 Ownership goes through change -1 \, so re-asserting it is free \, and a 0 to 1 transition sets dirty: while it was not ours the device redrew the surface. A bare change would swallow a first value of 0 as no change., f 50;
#X obj 20 1080 array define \$0-surface 109;
#X text 20 1140 The frame buffer \, one cell per Programmer Mode index. Cell 0 \, the Setup button \, is never written (item 110)., f 58;
#N canvas 30 30 1900 1000 disp-in 0;
#X text 20 20 One reserved selector on disp \, grid \, with this file's own vocabulary under it. C-5, f 58;
#X text 20 150 No list append before the second route: modal already arrives as the selector., f 58;
